IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-5.l4 -- ARTICLE 5: PRINCIPLES RELATING TO PROCESSING OF PERSONAL DATA.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Whose duty: Art 5(1) states what the personal data "shall be" and names no party; Art 5(2) puts
-- responsibility and the ability to demonstrate on the CONTROLLER.  Who may rely on it: the data
-- subject (the processing must meet each principle) and any supervisory authority.
-- Every principle is a function answering MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE = the principle is met on these
-- facts, JUST FALSE = it is not (the provision's own question; split site (i), NOTES.md).
-- "Lawfully", "fairly", "transparent", "adequate", "relevant", "appropriate" are judgments the text
-- leaves to the case: each is a plain input fact.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 5(1)(a): lawfulness, fairness and transparency`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:79 | (a) processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject (‘lawfulness, fairness and transparency’);
@ref Art 5(1)(a) (src:78-79)
GIVEN `the personal data are processed lawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are processed fairly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(a) the personal data are processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject` MEANS
    IF `the personal data are processed lawfully`
       AND `the personal data are processed fairly`
       AND `the personal data are processed in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: (a) processed lawfully, fairly and in a transparent manner in relation to the data subject"

§ `Article 5(1)(b): purpose limitation`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:80 | (b) collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes; further processing for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes shall, in accordance with Article 89(1), not be considered to be incompatible with the initial purposes (‘purpose limitation’);
@ref Art 5(1)(b), second limb: archiving, research and statistics (src:78-80)
GIVEN `the purpose of the further processing` IS AN `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics`
      `the further processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(b) the further processing is considered incompatible with the initial purposes` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the purpose of the further processing` EQUALS `Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose`)
       AND `the further processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat "shall ... not be considered"): "further processing for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes shall, in accordance with Article 89(1), not be considered to be incompatible with the initial purposes"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only further processing for those four purposes, in accordance with Article 89(1), is deemed not incompatible; for any other further processing the text leaves compatibility to the facts

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:80 | (b) collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes; further processing for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes shall, in accordance with Article 89(1), not be considered to be incompatible with the initial purposes (‘purpose limitation’);
@ref Art 5(1)(b) (src:78-80)
GIVEN `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are explicit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are legitimate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of the second limb` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(b) the personal data are collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are specified`
                AND `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are explicit`
                AND `the purposes for which the personal data are collected are legitimate`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: ... (b) collected for specified, explicit and legitimate purposes"
        IF `the personal data are further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes`
           AND NOT (`the answer of the second limb` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "and not further processed in a manner that is incompatible with those purposes"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 5(1)(c): data minimisation`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:81 | (c) adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed (‘data minimisation’);
@ref Art 5(1)(c) (src:78-81)
GIVEN `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(c) the personal data are adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed` MEANS
    IF `the personal data are adequate in relation to the purposes for which they are processed`
       AND `the personal data are relevant in relation to the purposes for which they are processed`
       AND `the personal data are limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: ... (c) adequate, relevant and limited to what is necessary in relation to the purposes for which they are processed"

§ `Article 5(1)(d): accuracy`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:82 | (d) accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date; every reasonable step must be taken to ensure that personal data that are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed, are erased or rectified without delay (‘accuracy’);
@ref Art 5(1)(d), first limb (src:78-82)
GIVEN `the personal data are accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are kept up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(d) the personal data are accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data are accurate`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: ... (d) accurate"
        IF `keeping the personal data up to date is necessary` AND NOT (`the personal data are kept up to date`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "and, where necessary, kept up to date"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:82 | (d) accurate and, where necessary, kept up to date; every reasonable step must be taken to ensure that personal data that are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed, are erased or rectified without delay (‘accuracy’);
@ref Art 5(1)(d), second limb (src:78-82)
GIVEN `some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 5(1)(d) every reasonable step is taken to ensure that inaccurate personal data are erased or rectified without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`some of the personal data are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the step is required for "personal data that are inaccurate, having regard to the purposes for which they are processed"; the clause is a scope limit with no gate word ("where", "if", "only"), so a case with no such data is outside it (periods ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F5-2 in NOTES.md, other reading `the duty does not arise`)
        IF `every reasonable step has been taken to erase or rectify the inaccurate personal data without delay`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "every reasonable step must be taken to ensure that personal data that are inaccurate ... are erased or rectified without delay"

§ `Article 5(1)(e): storage limitation`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:83 | (e) kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which the personal data are processed; personal data may be stored for longer periods insofar as the personal data will be processed solely for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1) subject to implementation of the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation in order to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject (‘storage limitation’);
@ref Art 5(1)(e), second limb (src:78-83)
GIVEN `the personal data will be processed solely for` IS AN `Art 5(1)(b) purpose of archiving, research or statistics`
      `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(e) the personal data may be stored for longer periods` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the personal data will be processed solely for` EQUALS `Art 5(1)(b) some other purpose`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a list closed with "solely"): "solely for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes"
        IF `the processing is in accordance with Article 89(1)`
           AND `the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation are implemented to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the function is named for a grant ("personal data may be stored for longer periods"), and the grant is limited by "in accordance with Article 89(1) subject to implementation of the appropriate technical and organisational measures"; neither "insofar as" nor "subject to" is a marker on which the text says no, so a case outside that limit is not covered (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1).
        -- One site, two answers (split site (ii), fork F5-3 in NOTES.md): the purpose arm is JUST FALSE because "solely" closes the list of purposes (limit 2); the other reading of the whole site is all JUST FALSE or all NOTHING.
        -- Outside the grant the first limb ("for no longer than is necessary") stands, and the function that tests it answers JUST FALSE for data kept longer without this exemption.

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:83 | (e) kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which the personal data are processed; personal data may be stored for longer periods insofar as the personal data will be processed solely for archiving purposes in the public interest, scientific or historical research purposes or statistical purposes in accordance with Article 89(1) subject to implementation of the appropriate technical and organisational measures required by this Regulation in order to safeguard the rights and freedoms of the data subject (‘storage limitation’);
@ref Art 5(1)(e) (src:78-83)
GIVEN `the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of the second limb` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(e) the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the personal data are kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- the sentence speaks of data "kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects"; data kept in a form that does not are not kept in such a form for any time
        IF NOT (`they are kept for longer than is necessary for the purposes for which they are processed`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer of the second limb` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: ... (e) kept in a form which permits identification of data subjects for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for which the personal data are processed"

§ `Article 5(1)(f): integrity and confidentiality`

-- src:78 | 1. Personal data shall be:
-- src:84 | (f) processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security of the personal data, including protection against unauthorised or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage, using appropriate technical or organisational measures (‘integrity and confidentiality’).
@ref Art 5(1)(f) (src:78-84)
GIVEN `the personal data are protected against unauthorised or unlawful processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are protected against accidental loss, destruction or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appropriate technical or organisational measures are used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1)(f) the personal data are processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security, using appropriate technical or organisational measures` MEANS
    IF `the personal data are protected against unauthorised or unlawful processing`
       AND `the personal data are protected against accidental loss, destruction or damage`
       AND `appropriate technical or organisational measures are used`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "Personal data shall be: ... (f) processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security of the personal data, including protection against unauthorised or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage, using appropriate technical or organisational measures"
    -- "including": the two protections are read as part of what "appropriate security" is (fork F5-4 in NOTES.md).

§ `Article 5(2): accountability`

DECLARE `Art 5(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 5(2) demonstrate compliance with paragraph 1`

-- src:85 | 2. The controller shall be responsible for, and be able to demonstrate compliance with, paragraph 1 (‘accountability’).
@ref Art 5(2), first limb: "shall be responsible for" (src:85)
GIVEN `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) the body is responsible for compliance with Art 5(1)` MEANS
    IF `the body is the controller`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text makes "The controller" responsible; it does not say whether anyone else is

-- src:85 | 2. The controller shall be responsible for, and be able to demonstrate compliance with, paragraph 1 (‘accountability’).
@ref Art 5(2), second limb: "be able to demonstrate compliance with, paragraph 1" (src:85)
GIVEN `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance` IS A LIST OF `Art 5 principle`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) the controller is able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` MEANS
    IF     elem `Art 5(1)(a) lawfulness, fairness and transparency` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
       AND elem `Art 5(1)(b) purpose limitation` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
       AND elem `Art 5(1)(c) data minimisation` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
       AND elem `Art 5(1)(d) accuracy` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
       AND elem `Art 5(1)(e) storage limitation` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
       AND elem `Art 5(1)(f) integrity and confidentiality` `the principles of Art 5(1) with which the controller can demonstrate compliance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "The controller shall be responsible for, and be able to demonstrate compliance with, paragraph 1"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the text names the party (the controller) and the act (demonstrate)
-- but states no time limit and no consequence, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:85 | 2. The controller shall be responsible for, and be able to demonstrate compliance with, paragraph 1 (‘accountability’).
@ref Art 5(2), regulative form (src:85)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 5(2) action`
`Art 5(2) the controller must be able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` MEANS
    PARTY `controller`
    MUST `Art 5(2) demonstrate compliance with paragraph 1`
    HENCE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 5(2) the controller must be able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 5(2) demonstrate compliance with paragraph 1` AT 10
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 5(2) the controller must be able to demonstrate compliance with Art 5(1)` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline in the text, so no breach).
